Richard,

Thanks for the discussion today. As agreed, the minutes-access pitch stays on=
 the reporting list for the October planning slot; it is not approved for pub=
lication. MIN-26-041 and MIN-26-042 are both still awaiting substantive respo=
nses. The 26-day median describes the first responses to the 14 earlier reque=
sts, not when people could see the minutes.

I've attached the review memo and the chart separating those responses from t=
he two open requests. Keith will pursue the Finance approval and posting reco=
rds; I'll follow the Clerk's index and circulation records for the work sessi=
on. We'll bring our progress together on October 5.

Leslie


